WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.034
-Guys, it can be hard to say
goodbye.

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.203
But sometimes you have to.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.503
And there are a few things
I would like to

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:08.140
say goodbye to right now.
It's time for "Go On, Git!"

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.343
[ Cheers and applause ]
-♪ Go on, git ♪

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.011
♪ Go on, git ♪

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:16.349
♪ Go on, go on, go on, git ♪

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.652 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.955 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:24.256
[ Country-western accent ]
Go on --

00:00:24.256 --> 00:00:27.026
Go on, git, eggnog!

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:31.063
What are you?
And why must you be so thick?

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.998
I don't know if I should
drink you,

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:35.267
pour you on a griddle
and make a pancake out of you,

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.571
or use you to fix a hole
in my roof like Flex Seal.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.873
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.474
I know you're
a Christmas tradition,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.809
so here's a concoction
that is sure to spice up

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.045
your next holiday party.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.613
It's one part eggnog,
12 parts rum,

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:50.283
dash of nutmeg,
and a twist of "Go on, git!"

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:54.353
[ Applause ]

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:56.422
Go on, git, November.

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:59.125
You're cold and you start
with the word "No."

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.460
That's two strikes in my book.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.896
If you were warm and started
with the word, "Yes,"

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.665
then heck,
I would be all about you.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.301
But that ain't the case.
So best go on, git, November,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.270
and don't come back until
you're "Yes-vem-warm."

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.475
[ Laughter ]
[ Scoffs ]

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.743
[ Desk thuds ]
[ Gasps ]

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.411
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.346
Ugh, that's my leg.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.681
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:23.882
Alright.

00:01:23.882 --> 00:01:25.451
[Desk door snaps shut]

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.487
Got bit off by a horse.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:30.490
-Right. [ Laughs ]

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.693
Go on, git, Bundt cake.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.561
I said it once,
I will say it again --

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:38.131
bunts are for baseball,
not bakeries,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.766
and, yeah, you I know
they're spelled different,

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:43.703
but I took your silent "D"
and snuck it in to another word,

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:47.439
"gidt" -- G-I-D-T, gidt.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:51.811
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.179
[ Spits ]
[ Tin clangs ]

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.682
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:56.749
[ Spits ]

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.850
[ Tin clangs ]

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:02.489
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.357
[ Spits ]

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.458
[ Tin clangs ]

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:09.362
Go on, git! Go on, git, tinsel!

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:13.299
Ye-- Look, Christmas trees,
I'm a fair guy.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.102
I will give you Christmas balls,
lights.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.103
Hell, I'll even give you
that string of popcorn

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:19.772
that nobody in real life
ever uses.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.609
But tinsel, you're just robot
spaghetti,

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.677
and you belong
in a robot restaurant

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.512
with the rest of
the robot pasta,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.748
so do me a favor
and [Robotic voice] go on, git!

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:34.220
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.657
[ Country-western accent ]
Go on, git, nonscented candles.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:41.393
If you don't smell like
pine trees or candy canes

00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:43.162
or gingerbread,
I don't need you.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:46.499
This isn't the 1700s. I ain't
looking for a light source.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.804
What I do need you for is to
provide a sniff for me to whiff,

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.172
a little whiff sniff.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:57.843
So, candles if you got no smell,
then you can go on to git.

00:02:57.843 --> 00:02:59.645
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:00.847
So hard to see 'em go,

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.715
but I'm glad I got them all
out of my system.

